---
title: One hire, end to end (no AD connection)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant HR as HR (source of truth)
    participant P as producer service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (backend)
    participant OA as OpenIAM A
    participant T as Transport (webhook / zip)
    participant RX as Other site (receiver)
    participant C as consumer service
    participant OB as OpenIAM B

    HR->>P: POST /producer/events {type: hire, employee_id: E1001, groups: [Finance], ...}
    P->>DB: lock "producer", seen event_id?
    alt resent message
        DB-->>P: stored result
        P-->>HR: 200 {duplicate: true}
    else new message
        P->>OA: search user employeeId=E1001
        OA-->>P: not found
        P->>OA: POST /prov/saveUser
        OA-->>P: status 200, contextValues.userId
        P->>OA: groups/search name=GRP-Finance-RW (alias), require managedSysId
        P->>OA: POST /prov/entitle ADD groupIds
        P->>DB: person state, memberships, activity log
        P->>DB: outbox: [create user E1001, add_member cn=GRP-Finance-RW]
        P-->>HR: 200 {ok: true, actions, instructions}
    end
    P->>T: deliver outbox in order (signed)
    T->>RX: instructions
    RX-->>T: 2xx = delivered (else retried with backoff)

    Note over P,OA: minutes later: change detection pulls OpenIAM A,<br/>sees the new user, emits an idempotent "create" (harmless repeat)

    P->>T: export: openiam-corp.example-...zip (changed domain only)
    T->>C: zip in inbox
    C->>C: verify sha256, reject stale / duplicate
    C->>OB: match employeeId=E1001, saveUser, groups
    C->>C: archive zip, log actions (visible in web)
